      "clause_id": "CPH-023",
      "end_character": 583,
      "excerpt": "A Canonical Package Home is the unique governed artifact tree H selected for an owner-local aggregate A by an explicit lifecycle-owner binding and unit-of-change declaration. H carries A's canonical machine sources. Capability, bounded-context, product, DomainSpec, implementation, evidence, and projection facets may be colocated in H when they share A's lifecycle, but their identities and authorities remain distinct and are connected by explicit typed relations. Indexes and global views may reference or generate projections of H; they must not duplicate its canonical carriers.",
